    "question": "What has concretely changed in AI coding agent tooling and infrastructure this month, and why does it matter for small teams?",
    "argument": "Several independent developments suggest that coding agents are moving from experimental add-ons toward infrastructure-level integration: Git platforms are rebuilding storage and branching systems to handle agent-volume commit rates; deployment tooling is being redesigned with agent lifecycle management as a first-class feature; secret-scanning pipelines are being replaced by purpose-built classifiers to keep pace with agent-generated code volume; and benchmark and evaluation tooling for agent code review is being published openly. Taken together, these changes shift the practical question for student teams from 'should I try an agent?' toward 'what governance and verification do I need before I do?' Each item is vendor-reported and warrants scrutiny, but the convergence across infrastructure, security, and evaluation layers is a candidate signal that the integration point has moved.",
